  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Levobunolol and Open-angle Glaucoma, mediated through Ocular Hypertension. This is supported by the shared indication of Ocular Hypertension in all three paths, which links Levobunolol to a series of drugs that ultimately target Open-angle Glaucoma. The presence of a consistent pathway from Levobunolol to Ocular Hypertension, and from Ocular Hypertension to Open-angle Glaucoma, indicates a possible mechanistic link. The scores from the paths are comparable, suggesting that the relationships are not coincidental but rather part of a broader network of drug–disease associations. The integration of these paths implies that Levobunolol may influence ocular pressure regulation, potentially contributing to the development of Open-angle Glaucoma. However, the exact mechanism remains unclear, and further experimental validation is needed to establish a direct causal relationship.",
